  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Women&apos;s participation in STEM activities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STEM hands-on activities for youth is experiential learning and is one of the most effective ways to develop the skills, mindsets, and competencies required for the 21st century. Hands-on activities move learning beyond theory, enabling young people to actively engage in problem-solving, experimentation, creativity, and critical thinking. Through practical STEM projects, innovation challenges, simulations, and community-based initiatives, youth are empowered to apply knowledge to real-world issues such as climate change, digital transformation, public health, and sustainable development.</narrative>
  </description>
